	(text "SERVO UART — CH344Q on hub port DS4 (USB 2.0 HS, UD+/UD- straight from the ESD array, no series resistors per WCH), four UARTs → servo-port-0..3.\nUART index ↔ physical port index is fixed by copper (software contract). 8 MHz ±0.4‰ crystal with 33 pF (20 pF CL), 100 nF on every VCC pin, TEST = GND.\nTNOW: a 4.7 k pull-down on each DTRx/TNOWx pin at power-up selects the TNOW function (CH344Q) and keeps the line low = receive when idle (ROBOTIS TX_Enable idle).\nRXD pull-ups live on the servo-port sheet next to the receivers (one 10 k per port; RXD3 has no internal pull-up). RESET: 10 k up + 100 nF, test point.\nACT (USB configured, active low) drives the green LED. Unused modem / GPIO pins left open (RTS0 and RTS3 must NOT be pulled down: they change pin functions).\nOpen items: V1 (TNOW polarity — scope the dongle), V2 (TNOW release latency vs Return Delay Time). Test points on every TXD / RXD / TNOW."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "14c36ff8-ab42-542b-8b11-b6d61871f7b4")
	)
	(text "Decoupling (one 100 nF per VCC pin + 10 µF)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 224.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eda5c9b2-ea10-5423-93ef-4b68811695a9")
	)
